    "title": "Phishing wave targeting xawilaad customers",
    "body": "Security notice — please share with your parents and aunties. There is an active phishing wave targeting xawilaad customers in Europe and North America. The pattern: an SMS or WhatsApp message claiming a transfer is “on hold”, linking to a fake xawilaad login page that harvests your details, sometimes followed by a call from a confident young man “from the office” who asks you to read back a code. Three things to remember: real xawilaad agents do not send login links; a one-time code is a key to your money and no legitimate employee ever needs it; and urgency is the attacker’s main tool — slow the conversation down. Ha gujin linkiga, ee dukaankaaga xawilaadda si toos ah u wac. If you or a relative already clicked: change the password, call your agent, and do not be ashamed — these operations are professional and they succeed against careful people every week. Fuller checklist coming in the Xawilaad Sandbox Lab.",
