    "title": "Macaan Bakery just hit 100 weekly orders — hiring our first delivery rider!",
    "body": "Three years ago I was baking halwa alone in my kitchen after Fajr and delivering it myself on a borrowed bike. This week, Macaan Bakery crossed 100 orders in one week for the first time. Alhamdulillah!\nThe breakdown, for my fellow food-business people: 55 walk-ins, 30 WhatsApp pre-orders, 15 custom cakes. The weekly kac kac subscription I was scared to launch? 22 subscribers, and it is now the most predictable revenue we have.\nAnd the scary exciting part: we are hiring our FIRST delivery rider. Eastleigh area, own motorbike, part-time mornings to start. If you know someone reliable — and I mean auntie-vouched reliable — send them my way.\nTo everyone here who told me to raise my prices last year: you were right. I said it. Alhamdulillah for this community.",
    "tags": [
      "food",
      "community"
    ],
