    "title": "Kickoff: why a sandbox, why now",
    "body": "Welcome to the Xawilaad Sandbox Lab — officially open. The idea in one paragraph: everyone wants to build on remittance rails, nobody can safely experiment on them, so we are building the practice field. A fake-money environment that behaves like the real thing: transfers, agent holds, payouts, failures, reconciliation. If a tool survives here, it has earned a conversation about real rails. What we are NOT doing: touching real money, storing real customer data, or pretending to be a licensed money transmitter — that is a decision, not an accident (see Lab decisions). Founding crew: me on API and product, @nasra_sec on security review, @sagal_ux on design, @cawo_cargo bringing the logistics-reconciliation brain, and @hamdi_agritech keeping us honest about offline-first. First milestone: a v0.1 test API with three endpoints and webhooks. Build logs weekly, in public, including the embarrassing parts. Soo dhawaada — bring questions, break things.",
