    "title": "Pricing workshop recap: what we covered and what surprised me",
    "body": "Recap of Tuesday's mentoring session for anyone who missed it. We worked through pricing for three member businesses: a tailoring service, a henna artist, and a snack seller. The pattern in all three: material costs were tracked to the shilling, but labour was priced at zero — 'my time is free because it is mine'. We built a simple rule together: count your hours, price them at what you would pay someone else to do the work, and if the market will not pay that price, the answer is changing the product, not deleting your wages. The worksheet we used is in the space files, in both languages. What surprised me: members pushed back hardest on charging for consultations and fittings — so the next session is entirely on pricing the invisible work. Thursday after next, same time.",
